.\" mask(1) — the shell entrance to the mask gateway.
.\"
.\" The version is substituted by packaging/debian/build-deb.sh; keep @VERSION@.
.TH mask 1 "" "mask @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mask \- PII pseudonymization gateway for local and cloud LLMs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mask
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mask
sits between a client and an LLM API. It detects personal data in the outgoing
request, replaces it with placeholders such as
.RB \(la 人名1 \(ra ,
and restores the original values in the answer. The upstream model receives
placeholders only.
.PP
The detection is offline: built\-in rules, a bundled name list and a dictionary
of your own terms, with no model download and no network call of its own. A
leak gate inspects every outgoing body and refuses the request when a value it
was supposed to mask is still present (\fBgateway.leak_gate = "block"\fR).
.PP
The binary covers both sides: \fBmask serve\fR runs the gateway, the other
commands are the human's entrance from a shell.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check \fR[\fITEXT\fR]...
Dry run: print the text as the model would receive it, with a table of what was
replaced. No network, no upstream key. Reads stdin when no text is given.
.TP
.B audit \fR[\fIFILES\fR]...
Dry run over files (\fB\-\fR is stdin). Prints the masked text plus line numbers
of spans that look like personal data but were not matched, so a miss is
visible instead of silent. \fB\-\-strict\fR exits 1 when such a span is found.
.TP
.B chat \fR[\fITEXT\fR]...
One prompt through the running gateway, with the answer restored. Options:
\fB\-\-model\fR (default \fIgpt\-4o\-mini\fR), \fB\-\-url\fR, \fB\-\-timeout\fR.
.TP
.B dict \fIadd\fR \fITERM\fR [\fITYPE\fR]
Register a term in the dictionary file. A running gateway merges additions
live; removals apply on restart.
.TP
.B dict \fIlist\fR
Print the registered terms.
.TP
.B dict \fIcheck\fR
Validate the dictionary file and report counts and line numbers. Values are
never printed.
.TP
.B status
Reliability panel of a running gateway: leak\-gate state, detection counts,
admin\-channel posture. \fB\-\-json\fR prints the raw \fB/status\fR body.
.TP
.B serve
Start the gateway. Binds \fB127.0.0.1:8080\fR unless configured otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIFILE\fR
Path to \fBmask.toml\fR. Default: \fB$MASK_CONFIG\fR, then
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mask/mask.toml\fR (\fB~/.config/mask/mask.toml\fR), then
\fB./mask.toml\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colours (also honoured from a pipe).
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-agent\-host
(\fBserve\fR only.) Start the gateway although this shell belongs to an AI
agent. The guard exists so that an agent cannot take over the operator's
instance, or read the upstream key out of the running process; this flag is the
human's deliberate override.
.TP
.B \-\-host \fIHOST\fR, \fB\-\-port \fIPORT\fR
(\fBserve\fR only.) Override the bind address from the config or environment.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mask/mask.toml
Operator's configuration, mode 600. Holds \fBupstream.api_key\fR and
\fBgateway.token\fR; keep it outside any checkout that an agent can read.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/mask/mask.toml.example
Every setting, with the environment variables that override it.
.TP
.I ./dictionary.tsv
Optional extra terms, one \fIterm\fR TAB \fItype\fR per line. The path comes
from \fBmask.dictionary\fR in the config.
.SH THE OPERATOR CHANNEL
\fB/admin/export\fR and \fB/admin/import\fR move the live pseudonym table
between gateways. They require \fBgateway.token\fR \fIand\fR a token minted at
startup and printed only to the gateway's own terminal, so a gateway started
without a terminal has no admin channel at all. Requests whose \fBHost\fR is
not a loopback address are refused (DNS rebinding).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mask check "山田太郎さんと 090\-1234\-5678 の件"
mask audit docs/*.md \-\-strict
mask dict add 取引先コード CUSTOM
mask serve                 # in your own terminal
export ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the command completed, including when \fBcheck\fR found personal data:
detection is the tool working, not a failure. 1 on an error, and for
\fBaudit \-\-strict\fR when a likely miss was found.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project page at \fIhttps://mask.branchead.com/\fR, and \fBmask.toml.example\fR
for the full configuration surface.
